{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01, which is about implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism.\n\nKey requirements from the candidate_artifact:\n1. For each call, subtract loss_with_call from loss_without_call to get the gain\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (at least one)\n3. Accept a call if it's parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\n5. Return accepted_call_ids and diagnostics with rounded normalized_gain\n\nLet me work through the logic:\n\nFor each call:\n- `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n- `normalized_gain = gain / max(prediction_tokens, 1)` (normalize by at least one prediction token)\n- `accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n\nThe output needs:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of call_id strings for accepted calls (in order)\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain` (rounded)\n\nThe \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. The schema says `normalized_gain` is a `number`, so I'll round to some reasonable precision. Looking at the fixture data, values are to 8 decimal places. Let me use `round(normalized_gain, 8)` or maybe less. Actually the instruction says \"rounded\" - I'll use standard Python rounding to a reasonable number of decimal places. Let me go with round to 6 decimal places or maybe just use the value as-is and round to 4 decimal places. Actually, the word \"rounded\" might just mean \"don't have infinite precision issues\" - I'll round to 6 decimal places.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The fixture has 8 decimal places in the input. Let me just round to a reasonable precision - maybe 8 decimal places to match the input precision.\n\nLet me verify with case 0:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595/5 = 0.3125312, threshold=0.05, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, threshold=0.05, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, threshold=0.05, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079 (approximately), threshold=0.05, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, normalized = 0.20983801/5 = 0.041967602, threshold=0.05, parseable=true, but 0.0419... \u003c 0.05 → NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, normalized = 0.76393214/4 = 0.190983035, threshold=0.05, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nFor case 2 (002):\n- call4: parseable=false → NOT accepted regardless\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Normalize by at least one prediction token\n        tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        # Accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold (inclusive)\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me verify once more and check if I need validation (ValueError for invalid cases):\n\nThe candidate_artifact says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\"\n\nI should add validation for required fields. Let me add basic validation.\n\nActually, for the purpose of this implementation, the key thing is to implement the core logic correctly. The strict submission envelope says my entire response must be exactly one valid JSON object with the single key \"implementation\" whose value is Python source.\n\nLet me write the final implementation:\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call at index {i} missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # Normalize by at least one prediction token\\n        tokens = max(prediction_tokens, 1)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain_rounded,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01fT3rQ1cGLoEsfEHUUdrZvp","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2504},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2504,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":15,"output_tokens":1765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1285},"service_tier":"standard"}}